  "worked_solution": "Let $P$ be the matrix that represents the rotation, $Q$ be the matrix that represents the shearing, and $R$ be the matrix that represents the reflection. These are given by the following elementary transformation matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(-\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & -\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(-\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}\u2061(-\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & \\operatorname{cos}\u2061(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ Q & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ R & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the combined transformation can be represented by the matrix $RQP:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RQP & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ -8 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$a+b=(-1)+1=0.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
